AMD Ryzen 5 5600. Godot Engine v4.3.stable.arch_linux - https://godotengine.org OpenGL API 4.6 (Core Profile) Mesa 24.3.3-arch1.2 - Compatibility - Using Device: AMD - AMD Radeon RX 5700 (radeonsi, navi10, LLVM 19.1.6, DRM 3.59, 6.12.10-zen1-1-zen)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using `autowrap` and `horizontal expand` at the same time, the button is rendered in a reduced size and the text goes beyond the edges. But if you twitch the window, everything becomes fine.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a10f6b2c-357f-4b35-963d-f3c3e3a2355a)\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI made a short video in which I reproduce the bug\n[video on youtube](https://youtu.be/e7jOtUAEAVg)\n[video on github](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/02b8dde6-9c29-47f0-8b23-936cd12b4a8f)\n\n\nIf you try to explain it in words, you need to create a `GridContainer` and set 2 columns. Then you need to put 2 buttons in it and set `autowrap` and `horizontal expand` for them. You need to add a lot of text to the buttons IN ONE LINE. We launch the project and see how our text goes beyond the button, but as soon as we slightly change the window size, everything becomes fine\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18482595/test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Randommist","id":70176501,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTc2NTAx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70176501?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Randommist","html_url":"https://github.com/Randommist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Randommist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Randommist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Randommist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Randommist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Randommist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Randommist/orgs","